1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,891
Which one did the officer read?

2
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:05,697
It came back with one word: resubmit.

3
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:09,058
Which document? Which section? Everything, again.

4
00:00:09,410 --> 00:00:10,967
So I built PermitFlow.

5
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:14,712
The check finds an expired certificate before you submit.

6
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:19,338
Submit once. The application is recorded as Revision 1.

7
00:00:21,810 --> 00:00:25,138
It appears in the officer's queue, with the checks already run.

8
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:32,381
Now, the officer's side: the same finding, and the evidence behind it.

9
00:00:32,730 --> 00:00:36,847
Feedback points at the exact document, not at the whole application.

10
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:41,790
Only the flagged parts reopen.

11
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:46,999
One file replaced, one click: Revision 2 is recorded.

12
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:51,425
Back with the officer, the item is already marked addressed.

13
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:56,409
After the site visit, approval issues the licence. Every step on record.

14
00:00:57,050 --> 00:01:04,346
Checked before submission. Feedback tied to the document. Only the flagged parts reopened. Every step on record.

15
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:07,469
Checks help you. Officers decide.
